ef 1071 "Identify the equation that corresponds to the graph below.\n\n![](images/43/438de2ca2258d658868c730115b7d30d99aa46193accd6478f7400486b8db1f5.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ff34ddfb-7ea8-505a-8a4f-7898d7f5c3c0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054390 #edb/ref 1074 "The graph is a horizontal line where the $y$-value of every point is $-1$. Consequently, its equation is $y = -1$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054391 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12903" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054391 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/45/45ba98becc788f2c39f7e03b13b021beebce36e8cf3c8f50299bdfba041dfff4.png)\n\nWhich of the plots above shows the following lines?\n\n- $x=-1$\n- $y=-1$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054391 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "1af37b2d-2400-5e55-b7b6-6d9652204f4c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054391 #edb/ref 1074 "- On the line $x=-1$, every point has an $x$-coordinate of $-1$. Therefore, graph II represents this equation.\n- On the line $y=-1$, every point has an $y$-coordinate of $-1$. Therefore, graph III represents this equation." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054392 #edb/ref 1069 "e-12904" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054392 #edb/ref 1071 "A horizontal line in the $xy$-plane passes through the point $(-2,4)$. What is the equation of the line? Does the point $(4,-2)$ lie on that line?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054392 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "03ebd3ab-aa4d-5bf4-9079-62cde6da307d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054392 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the horizontal line passes through $(-2,4)$, every point on the line has a $y$-coordinate of $4$. So, the equation of that line is $y=4$.\n\nThe $y$-coordinate of the point $(4,-2)$ is $-2$, but all points on the line $y=4$ have a $y$-coordinate of $4$. So, the point $(4,-2)$ is not on the line.\n\n![](images/0f/0fa994fe8d3da1428d803aa0c6d6c1470eab0fd23e24cd0edd67bb213efec068.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186054491 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1