ef 1061 191798 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055621 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4925b445-d5c7-5a6b-a5f1-da050fb02303" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055621 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056014 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055622 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055622 #edb/ref 1061 191799 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055622 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2922d040-74f4-5896-83b7-35b38603c224" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055622 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054666 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055623 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055624 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055623 #edb/ref 1061 191802 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055623 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3e8762cd-7d9e-50f2-bb1b-c07fd53a30c1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055623 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186056015 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055624 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055625 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055624 #edb/ref 1061 191803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055624 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "95b8d112-1200-5651-b046-ddd819995d89" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055624 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054667 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055625 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186055626 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055625 #edb/ref 1061 191806 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055625 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f599f285-d643-5707-ac7a-89a8993f9002" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055625 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055626 #edb/ref 1061 191809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055626 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30da6f5a-53a7-5a1c-9b14-200b76e84b56" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186055626 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186054669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186056014 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose that we wish to find the equation of the **horizontal line** that passes through the point $(0,3)$, as shown below:\n\n![](images/37/379af2ba930fa537f1fbdda5b4b5cc91e355a46e90918cdc56bbce66f3502d7b.png)\n\nNotice that for